    <!-- Phase 9: Help screen -->
    <string name="help_q_import">How do I import Google Timeline JSON?</string>
    <string name="help_a_import">Tap Create Video on the Home screen, choose your Timeline.json with the system file picker, and the app parses it on-device. Your original file is never modified or deleted.</string>
    <string name="help_q_formats">Which Timeline formats are supported?</string>
    <string name="help_a_formats">The app reads the timelinePath / semantic segments format exported by Google Takeout (Location History). Files that cannot be parsed show a clear error with the reason instead of a blank screen.</string>
    <string name="help_q_noname">Why is a location name missing?</string>
    <string name="help_a_noname">Place names come from a bundled offline city dataset. A stop shows \u201cLocation unavailable\u201d when no known city is within range \u2014 the raw coordinates are still used for the map and the video.</string>
    <string name="help_q_style">Why does a map style differ by provider/device?</string>
    <string name="help_a_style">Map styles are real tile layers: Standard (CARTO), Satellite and Hybrid (Esri imagery), Terrain (OpenTopoMap). If tiles cannot load \u2014 for example offline \u2014 the map shows an offline notice instead of fake imagery.</string>
    <string name="help_q_render">How does video generation work?</string>
    <string name="help_a_render">The preview and the export share one deterministic animation: each video frame is computed from the frame timestamp, then rendered with the device encoder (H.264) into an MP4. Rendering runs in the background and survives navigation; you can cancel it at any time.</string>
    <string name="help_q_where">Where are generated videos saved?</string>
    <string name="help_a_where">In Movies/Timeline Visualizer on this device, managed through Android\u2019s MediaStore. They appear in My Videos with a thumbnail, duration, resolution, and the journey\u2019s date range.</string>
    <string name="help_q_rename">How do I rename a saved video?</string>
    <string name="help_a_rename">Open the video in My Videos, tap Rename, and enter a name. Renaming updates the display name in your library; the underlying video file stays exactly where it is.</string>
    <string name="help_q_delete">How do I delete a generated video?</string>
    <string name="help_a_delete">Open the video, tap Delete, and confirm. The app deletes the actual video file first, then removes its thumbnail and library entry. If the file cannot be deleted, the library entry is kept so you don\u2019t lose track of it.</string>
    <string name="help_q_missing">Why can a generated video be missing from History?</string>
    <string name="help_a_missing">If the video file was removed outside the app (for example in the Files app), the library removes the stale entry automatically the next time it loads. The app never deletes your other files.</string>
    <string name="help_q_upload">Is my Timeline uploaded?</string>
    <string name="help_a_upload">No. Import, place-name resolution, and video rendering all happen on this device. The only network use is downloading map tiles. See the Privacy screen for details.</string>
    <string name="help_q_tracking">Does the app track my current location?</string>
    <string name="help_a_tracking">No. It visualizes historical coordinates from the file you import. It does not request location permission and has no background location tracking.</string>

